target:    src/Tracker/Session.php
gate:      php tests/anonymous-identity-test.php
kind:      name-only
expect:    nothing checks probeFailed()
rationale: Use the probe form and throw its verdict away. probeVar() is still called, so a gate asserting the name appears passes - and the null it returns is once again indistinguishable from "this visitor has no previous hit". Before AddVisitIdentity runs, vid_hash does not exist and that is EVERY hit: each anonymous pageview mints a fresh visit_id and visits inflate to roughly pageviews for the whole pre-migration window, silently.
---
--- a/src/Tracker/Session.php
+++ b/src/Tracker/Session.php
@@ -302,16 +302,7 @@
 
 		$existing_visit_id = $probe->probeVar();
 
-		if ($probe->probeFailed()) {
-			// Before AddVisitIdentity runs, vid_hash does not exist and this SELECT errors.
-			// Read as "no previous hit", which is what a bare null meant, every anonymous
-			// pageview mints a fresh visit_id — so visits inflate to roughly pageviews for
-			// the whole pre-migration window, silently. Say so once per request instead.
-			self::recordIdentityProbeFailure();
 
-			return 0;
-		}
-
 		return $existing_visit_id > 0 ? intval($existing_visit_id) : 0;
 	}
 
